<title>THAILAND: Thai Farmers to manage PTT provident fund.</title>
<headline>Thai Farmers to manage PTT provident fund.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Farmers Bank said on Monday it signed an agreement to co-manage a provident fund worth 2.4 billion baht ($93.02 million) of the state-run Petroleum Authority of Thailand (PTT).</p>
<p>Banthoon Lamsam, president of Thailand's third largest bank, said the other co-manager of the three-year-old fund was Phatra Thanakit Plc.</p>
<p>A total of 3,120 employees of PTT will join the provident fund scheme, Banthoon said.</p>
<p>To date, the bank manages 20 provident funds worth 3.625 billion baht, a bank spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>($1 = 25.80)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
